ve to go through moments  where you're not always on in order to  get stronger and to grow so  100% as I understand a lot of the music  in this album comes from like the  conflicting emotions that you've had  over the last few years mixed emotions  something has to do with a with a  breakup that you had recently then this  is your ex heard any of the music that  might be about yeah everybody everybody  I write about hears it before I put it  out just because it's like I choose to  write these things but they don't choose  to have you know aspects of their life  in a song so like everybody I write  about whether it's even like my parents  or my brother like even small lines I  always say like is this okay so yes he's  heard of everyone's heard them is it  more nerve-wracking to share that you  know those lines of those songs with the  people that are close to you more so  than all the millions of strangers  that'd be listening a little bit yeah it  actually is because I guess that you  don't really know all the strangers and  you don't you don't have to watch them  listening but usually when I play  something for somebody close to me I'm  usually there with them or they give me  direct feedback and you know it's like  you're you're opening up in a way that  you might not have like just by talking  to them so then like a lot of the songs  for Milo and I play them for my parents  it's like they were finding out things  that I don't ever really say to them so  which is like weird or like whether it's  a the relationship or things like that  like that's how I express myself so I  might have jotted down some things that  I actually never said which can be kind  of scary but with regards to to that  acts like how does he take the music was  surprised like what was the emotional  state uh I don't know I guess well I  don't know if he was lying I said he  said he likes it a lot I don't know if  they're I mean I don't know if anyone's  lying when they I don't I trust him I  trust everybody that I that's like close  to me and we're still we're still really  close I think you like they I don't I  don't I don't ever like write songs to  to be mean or say things like I just  write how I feel so I hope it's not like  offensive to anybody who do you trust  like that's close to you to be honest  with you about your music about the  views that you're putting out to tell  you like hmm I'm not feeling that hook  or whatever um I usually I usually send  them to my best friend  who usually like she has like a really  good ear and she has really good music  taste I think so I always trust her and  my parents honestly and my manager I  have like just my core group of people I  really just trust their ear in their  opinion so I'll try to like show them  everything yeah that core group is so  important yeah are you ever concerned  about I just get bigger and you go on in  your career sort of losing focus losing  who you are and who you've wanted to be  I mean I guess sometimes it can be it  can be easy to be skewed one way or  another when you're in this industry but  I think I'm such a stubborn person to be  honest or if people try to tell me to do  something or be something I'm not I'm  gonna like do the opposite even more to  prove why they're wrong you know so in  that sense I mean I don't really fear it  it is like something that you kind of  have to battle with every day cuz you're  gonna have all these voices and opinions  and things like that but I'm not worried  of changing because I feel like I have a  strong idea of at least who I am I don't  know a lot of things and I'm still  figuring out a million and one things  about myself but I Know Who I am and  that's the most important thing do you  feel like you're living your dream right  now yeah definitely and more I didn't  even know what that dream entailed I  just knew I wanted to do music you know  so there's so much more that comes with  that that I didn't even know I loved so  yeah defini